### Play dirty: Level 3
**Prepare.** When you use the *Steady Aim* feature, you gain the benefit of advantage until the end of your next turn, but you still lose it immediately after the attack.

>**Focus and Wait.** When you use the *Dodge* action, you can trade the disadvantage imposed on attacks against you to instead eliminate the disadvantage imposed on attacks made using the Countermeasures feature. However, instead of imposing disadvantage on attack rolls against you, you can choose to grant advantage on attack rolls against you, thereby gaining advantage for attacks from your Countermeasures feature.

### Improved Evasions: Level 9
If you use your reaction in response to being targeted by an attack roll, taking damage from an attack, taking damage from a spell, or being targeted by a spell, you can use your Countermeasures feature as part of the same reaction, provided all applicable rules are met and the original reaction involves reducing damage or making an attack roll. Succeeding on a Dexterity save throw counts as an available trigger, by the target, for the purposes of *Counter-Attack*, and failing counts as a trigger for *Parry*(if wielding a shield, only).


### I Fought Against Equals: Level 13
If you spend at least 1 minute observing or interacting with another creature outside combat, you can learn certain information about its capabilities compared to your own. The DM tells you if the creature is your equal, superior, or inferior in regard to two of the following characteristics of your choice:

- Higher total bonus for attack rolls
- Armor Class
- Dexterity score
- Current hit points
- Total class levels or challenge rating, if any
  
### Flash and Roll: Level 13
You gain 1,5 meters of extra movement. This movement does not provoke attacks of opportunity. You can choose not to spend this move on your turn, saving it to use immediately after your Improved Evasion or Countermeasures features; however, if your movement 

