ends behind cover, you can apply the cover bonus to any Dexterity saving throws and to your Armor Class, potentially preventing the harmful consequence that triggered the reaction.







### Inopportune Condition: Level 17
You have learned to spot patterns in your opponents and exploit their weaknesses. When you hit an attack against a target that you can see in any of these contexts, it is considered an *Exposed* target:
- Prone
- Incapacitated
- Restrained
- Taked a stealthy melee hit in this attack
- Taked a critical hit in this attack
- Rolled a *critical failure* against you this round (this mark expires after this hit)
  


Hitting a target marked as **Exposed** imposes it to make a Constitution saving throw against your *Combatant Save DC*. If an Exposed target fails the check, it take +10 additional **damage** of the weapon's type and becomes **prone**.

>**Combatant save DC** = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier

&emsp; 

{{note
##### Stealth
You are stealthy if you succeed in a stealth check contested by the target's passive perception.

##### Exposed
Exclusive mark for functionalities of this subclass. It is **not** shared with others in combat.

}}
### Champion Duelist: Level 17
You have mastered the art of combat and dueling through training and supernatural agility. You can change one of the following combat stances at the start of your turn, but only once per round. You can only have one active instance at a time.

**Dasher.** The reach of your weapons is increased by 1,5 meters.

**Deadeye.** You can use your Counter-Attack feature against targets up to 15 meters away, and the trigger becomes: When another creature misses an attack against a target at this distance, provided you can see both targets. This is compatible with Improved Evasion.

**Consultant.** If you hit the target, you learn one characteristic from your I Fought Against Equals feature.


\column

&emsp;**Plunger.** You gain advantage on Dexterity saving throws and you can jump 1,5 meters higher. If you jump from a height that would cause falling damage and land on an enemy, you can use your reaction to make an attack roll while falling. If you hit, you transfer half the falling damage you would have taken to the enemy and can roll your Sneak Attack die.

&emsp;Additionally, if you are hit by a critical hit, you can choose to treat the attack roll as a normal hit; and the attacker is then considered Exposed until the end of you next turn. You can use this feature once per long rest.

